---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { LIMITS } from "../lib/api";
import { QUICKNET, roundForTime, roundTime } from "../lib/drand";

const exRound = roundForTime(Date.parse("2026-10-22T01:05:03Z"));
const exUnlock = new Date(roundTime(exRound)).toISOString();
const exUnix = roundTime(exRound) / 1000;
const kib = (n: number) => `${(n / 1024).toLocaleString("en-US")} KiB`;
const mib = (n: number) => `${n / 1024 / 1024} MiB`;
const errors: [number, string, string][] = [
	[400, "invalid_json", "Body isn't a JSON object."],
	[400, "invalid_request", "A field is missing or invalid; `message` says which."],
	[403, "forbidden", "Cross-origin call to an endpoint reserved for the website."],
	[405, "method_not_allowed", "Wrong HTTP method."],
	[413, "payload_too_large", "Body or plaintext over the limit; includes `limitBytes`."],
	[422, "invalid_ciphertext", "Not a tlock age ciphertext, or it's corrupted."],
	[422, "unsupported_chain", "Ciphertext was made for a drand chain other than quicknet."],
	[425, "too_early", "Unlock round not reached yet; includes `round`, `unlockAt`, `unlockAtUnix`."],
	[500, "internal_error", "Unexpected server error."],
	[502, "drand_unavailable", "No drand relay answered. Retry with backoff."],
	[503, "feed_unavailable", "The activity feed database isn't configured."],
];
---

<Base title="API · timelock.dev" description="JSON API for timelock encryption: encrypt and decrypt messages tied to drand quicknet rounds. Includes curl examples, schemas, errors and limits.">
	<div class="container narrow prose">
		<h1>API</h1>
		<p class="muted">
			Base URL <code>https://timelock.dev</code>. No authentication. CORS is open (<code>Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *</code>), so you can call it
			from any site.
		</p>

		<div class="callout small">
			<strong>The server sees your plaintext.</strong> These endpoints encrypt and decrypt on our Worker, so the plaintext passes through it in
			memory. It's never logged or stored, but you have to trust that. For anything sensitive, use the
			<a href="/">website</a> (encrypts in your browser) or a <a href="/how-it-works#cli">local CLI</a>. Both produce identical, interchangeable
			ciphertext.
		</div>

		<nav aria-label="Endpoints" class="small">
			<ul>
				<li><a href="#encrypt"><code>POST /api/encrypt</code></a>: encrypt to a duration, date or round</li>
				<li><a href="#decrypt"><code>POST /api/decrypt</code></a>: decrypt once the round is reached</li>
				<li><a href="#events"><code>GET /api/events</code></a>: the public activity feed</li>
				<li><a href="#legacy"><code>POST /encrypt/:round</code> and <code>POST /decrypt</code></a>: original raw-bytes endpoints</li>
				<li><a href="#errors">Errors</a> · <a href="#limits">Limits</a></li>
			</ul>
		</nav>

		<h2 id="encrypt">POST /api/encrypt</h2>
		<p>Encrypts a message so it can only be decrypted at or after a drand quicknet round. Give exactly one of <code>duration</code>, <code>unlockAt</code> or <code>round</code>.</p>
		<pre><code>curl -s https://timelock.dev/api/encrypt \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '&#123;"plaintext": "hello, future", "duration": "5m"&#125;'</code></pre>

		<h3>Request body</h3>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td><code>plaintext</code></td><td>string, required</td><td>The message. Up to {kib(LIMITS.plaintextBytes)} after decoding.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>encoding</code></td><td><code>"utf8"</code> | <code>"base64"</code></td><td>How <code>plaintext</code> is encoded. Default <code>"utf8"</code>. Use base64 for binary data.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>duration</code></td><td>number | string</td><td>Seconds from now (<code>300</code>) or a duration string: <code>"90s"</code>, <code>"15m"</code>, <code>"2h30m"</code>, <code>"3 days 6 hours"</code>. Units: s, m, h, d, w, y (365 days).</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>unlockAt</code></td><td>number | string</td><td>Unix seconds, or ISO 8601 with a time zone: <code>"2030-01-01T00:00:00Z"</code>, <code>"2030-01-01T09:00:00+09:00"</code>. Must be in the future.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>round</code></td><td>integer</td><td>An exact quicknet round. Past rounds are allowed; the result is decryptable immediately.</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<p class="small muted">Times are rounded <em>up</em> to the next round (one every {QUICKNET.period} seconds), so <code>unlockAt</code> in the response can be up to {QUICKNET.period} s later than requested. The maximum is {LIMITS.maxUnlockSeconds / (365 * 86400)} years ahead.</p>

		<h3>Response <code>200</code></h3>
		<pre><code>&#123;
  "ciphertext": "-----BEGIN AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----\nYWdlLWVuY3J5cHRpb24ub3JnL3YxCi0+IHRsb2Nr…\n-----END AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----\n",
  "round": {exRound},
  "unlockAt": "{exUnlock}",
  "unlockAtUnix": {exUnix},
  "chainHash": "{QUICKNET.hash}",
  "network": "quicknet"
&#125;</code></pre>

		<h3>More examples</h3>
		<pre><code># unlock at a specific moment
curl -s https://timelock.dev/api/encrypt \
  -d '&#123;"plaintext": "Happy new year!", "unlockAt": "2030-01-01T00:00:00Z"&#125;'

# binary data, ciphertext saved to a file (needs jq)
curl -s https://timelock.dev/api/encrypt \
  -d "&#123;\"plaintext\": \"$(base64 -w0 photo.jpg)\", \"encoding\": \"base64\", \"duration\": \"30d\"&#125;" \
  | jq -r .ciphertext > photo.jpg.age</code></pre>

		<h2 id="decrypt">POST /api/decrypt</h2>
		<p>Decrypts a ciphertext once its round has been published. Accepts anything produced by this site, the API, <code>dee</code>, <code>tlock</code> or <code>tlock-js</code> for quicknet (armored form).</p>
		<pre><code>curl -s https://timelock.dev/api/decrypt \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d "$(jq -Rs '&#123;ciphertext: .&#125;' message.age)"</code></pre>
		<h3>Request body</h3>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td><code>ciphertext</code></td><td>string, required</td><td>Armored age text, <code>-----BEGIN AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----</code> … <code>-----END AGE ENCRYPTED FILE-----</code>.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>encoding</code></td><td><code>"base64"</code></td><td>Optional. Force base64 output even when the plaintext is valid UTF-8.</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<h3>Response <code>200</code></h3>
		<pre><code>&#123;
  "plaintext": "hello, future",
  "encoding": "utf8",
  "round": {exRound},
  "unlockAt": "{exUnlock}",
  "unlockAtUnix": {exUnix}
&#125;</code></pre>
		<p class="small">Plaintext that isn't valid UTF-8 comes back as base64 with <code>"encoding": "base64"</code>.</p>
		<h3>Too early: <code>425</code></h3>
		<pre><code>&#123;
  "error": &#123;
    "code": "too_early",
    "message": "Too early: this message unlocks at drand round {exRound} ({exUnlock}).",
    "round": {exRound},
    "unlockAt": "{exUnlock}",
    "unlockAtUnix": {exUnix}
  &#125;
&#125;</code></pre>

		<h2 id="events">GET /api/events</h2>
		<p>The public activity feed, newest first. It contains no message content, ciphertext or IP addresses.</p>
		<pre><code>curl -s 'https://timelock.dev/api/events?limit=2'</code></pre>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th>Query</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					<tr><td><code>limit</code></td><td>1 to {LIMITS.feedPageSize}, default 20.</td></tr>
					<tr><td><code>before</code></td><td>Return events with an id lower than this (pagination: pass the previous <code>nextBefore</code>).</td></tr>
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		<pre><code>&#123;
  "events": [
    &#123;
      "id": 42,
      "type": "decrypt",
      "source": "api",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T01:06:10.512Z",
      "round": {exRound},
      "unlockAt": "{exUnlock}"
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      "id": 41,
      "type": "encrypt",
      "source": "web",
      "createdAt": "2026-10-22T01:00:01.204Z",
      "round": {exRound},
      "unlockAt": "{exUnlock}"
    &#125;
  ],
  "nextBefore": 41
&#125;</code></pre>
		<p class="small"><code>source</code> is <code>"web"</code> (browser-side, reported by the website after the fact) or <code>"api"</code> (recorded by the server). <code>nextBefore</code> is <code>null</code> on the last page. Responses may be cached for 5 seconds. <code>POST /api/events</code> is used by the website itself and only accepts same-origin requests.</p>

		<h2 id="legacy">Original endpoints</h2>
		<p>The endpoints of the original Rust worker still work unchanged for existing scripts: raw bytes in, raw bytes out, no JSON. Uploads can be up to {mib(LIMITS.legacyBodyBytes)}.</p>
		<h3>POST /encrypt/:round</h3>
		<p>Body: the raw plaintext (any bytes). Response: armored age ciphertext (<code>Content-Type: application/octet-stream</code>). Look up the round for a time with <code>/api/encrypt</code> or <code>dee</code>.</p>
		<pre><code>curl -s -X POST --data-binary @original.png https://timelock.dev/encrypt/{exRound} > encrypted.age</code></pre>
		<h3>POST /decrypt</h3>
		<p>Body: armored <em>or</em> binary age ciphertext. Response: the raw plaintext bytes.</p>
		<pre><code>curl -s -X POST --data-binary @encrypted.age https://timelock.dev/decrypt > decrypted.png</code></pre>
		<p class="small">Errors on these endpoints are plain text with the HTTP status codes listed below (for example <code>425</code> when it's too early).</p>

		<h2 id="errors">Errors</h2>
		<p>JSON endpoints return <code>&#123;"error": &#123;"code": "…", "message": "…"&#125;&#125;</code> with extra fields where noted.</p>
		<div class="table-wrap">
			<table>
				<thead><tr><th>Status</th><th>Code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					{errors.map(([status, code, meaning]) => <tr><td>{status}</td><td><code>{code}</code></td><td>{meaning}</td></tr>)}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>

		<h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
		<ul>
			<li>JSON plaintext: {kib(LIMITS.plaintextBytes)} after decoding; JSON request body: {kib(LIMITS.jsonBodyBytes)}.</li>
			<li>Original endpoints: {mib(LIMITS.legacyBodyBytes)} per request. For larger files, encrypt locally with <code>dee</code>; there's no size limit there.</li>
			<li>Unlock time: up to {LIMITS.maxUnlockSeconds / (365 * 86400)} years ahead, at {QUICKNET.period}-second granularity.</li>
			<li>Network: drand quicknet only, chain hash <code>{QUICKNET.hash}</code>.</li>
			<li>Cloudflare may rate-limit abusive traffic. Please back off on <code>502</code>.</li>
		</ul>
	</div>
</Base>
